# ── Replit agent & task internal state (never commit to public repos) ─────────
# `.agents/*` (not `.agents/`): git cannot re-include files under an EXCLUDED
# PARENT DIRECTORY, so with the directory form the `!.agents/skills/**` negations
# below were inert — a brand-new skill file was invisible to `git add -A` and
# would silently never ship. Excluding the directory's *contents* keeps the
# same coverage while letting the skills/README negations actually work.
.agents/*
.local/
skills-lock.json
attached_assets/

# `.agents/skills/` and `.agents/README.md` are real, tracked AGENTS.md
# playbooks (see AGENTS.md "Agent Skills") despite the blanket rule above.
!.agents/skills/
!.agents/skills/**
!.agents/README.md

# ── Claude Code harness runtime state (never commit) ───────────────────────────
.claude/worktrees/

# ── Temporary / scratch ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.tmp
*.temp
INSTRUCTIONS.md
